{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/631355-idigam-and-moon-invading-techno-demons","id":631355,"title":"Idigam and Moon Invading Techno Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T11:53:06-07:00","id":631355,"title":"Idigam and Moon Invading Techno Demons","content":"So, the situation...<br /> <br /> A Demon (Unchained, as in Demon the Descent), in 5300BC or so, has arrived on the moon. Father Wolf mistook the Demon for an Idigam and dropped it on the surface of the moon.<br /> <br /> An unformed Idigam examined the newly-ditched Demon and is now trying to coalesce based upon form it now can observe. The Demon has a virtue of Curiosity and a Vice of Utilitarian Thinking.<br /> <br /> What sort of horrible creature might emerge from such a strange union?<br /> <br /> I have no idea so I come to the masters for help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T05:45:35-07:00","id":647898,"title":"","content":"What is the Idigam's purpose in the story? Is it a force of nature-type villain, or is it going to be more intimate, with a personal vendetta vs. the PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7353-voragosolitude","name":"VoragoSolitude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7353_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T10:02:15-07:00","id":648112,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble understanding the premise. Was Father Wolf already in the surface of the Moon? (Why?)<br /> <br /> Was it an unchained, or an Angel? Because really, the former is a corporeal entity, the other is an ethereal one, and even then, it would be difficult to mistake an Angel for a spirit. We're talking about the personification of the Hunt. He'd probably smell the stench of an occult matrix on an angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T10:26:27-07:00","id":648122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/631355-idigam-and-moon-invading-techno-demons?p=648112#post648112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble understanding the premise. Was Father Wolf already in the surface of the Moon? (Why?)</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise of the Moon-Banished myth is that the idigam were hurled to Luna's surface by Urfarah after he recognized that no Earthly prison could hold them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T10:37:19-07:00","id":648133,"title":"","content":"And since Urfarah didn't just hunt spirits it's entirely possible it smelled the scent of whatever the Demon had and went on hunting. Piff said it was a Demon, so it's not an angel.<br /> <br /> I guess the obvious thing would be an emulation of a Demon. Which would be weird, because you have three layers of a fallen being going on there. Alternatively, however, you could look at the individual things that a Demon does and go from there. It could attempt to become a sort of anthropomorphic being striving after the Demon's agenda, or something that mindlessly deals in souls, blending in from some unseen enemy. It could even take ideas from what the Demon is running away from, trying to build itself as a mock God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T11:36:11-07:00","id":648199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/631355-idigam-and-moon-invading-techno-demons?p=648122#post648122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise of the Moon-Banished myth is that the idigam were hurled to Luna's surface by Urfarah after he recognized that no Earthly prison could hold them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that. Read how OP phrased that again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T13:47:54-07:00","id":648318,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the God-Machine have infrastructure on the Moon already? I mean, one of the Apollo missions brought something back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that. Read how OP phrased that again. </div> </div> </div>It's slightly oddly constructed but it's not incorrect. The first sentence tells you where and when the Demon is located. The second sentence tells you how it got there. Father Wolf is only on the Moon if you assume the two sentences are giving details in chronological order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T14:26:11-07:00","id":648353,"title":"","content":"If you take some of the stories in the GMC as canon, yeah, there was something on the moon God Machine-wise.<br /> <br /> Also, The result would be hard to imagine. I have no ideas coming to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-01-2015, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T23:17:18-07:00","id":648591,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the corpse of an angel, supposedly. <br /> <br /> Kind of hinted it's a corpse in the &quot;That is not dead that can eternal lie, And with strange aeons even death may die&quot; sort of way, but maybe it's just a particularly strange bit of infrastructure. <br /> <br /> So what I would do is have an idigam (or more) hitching a ride with the secret NASA mission to retrieve the angel corpse, so the idigam(s) would probably soak up space exploration, government conspiracy, and dead angel vibes, so it (or they) would be strange even by idigam levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:31:26-07:00","id":649059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/631355-idigam-and-moon-invading-techno-demons?p=648112#post648112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was it an unchained, or an Angel? Because really, the former is a corporeal entity, the other is an ethereal one, and even then, it would be difficult to mistake an Angel for a spirit. We're talking about the personification of the Hunt. He'd probably smell the stench of an occult matrix on an angel.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unchained was examined and spoofed. The spoof, being an infallible method of deception, managed to convince Wolf that the being looked absolutely human.<br /> <br /> Of course from context Wolf knew that wasn't the case, but what he was left with was the following information : this thing can look like a human, can imitate humans, but is not human, and is probably not a spirit in the conventional sense of the word.<br /> <br /> So, basically, this was a situation created by assumptions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:11:57-07:00","id":649096,"title":"","content":"Well, here's the thing about dropping a demon on the moon. It would die very quickly. Lets pretend that we have a Demonic Form part that lets it survive in Space (the Environmental Resistance should work). That still doesn't let the demon's human Cover survive for long - it still needs food and water. So, the Demon is forced to shift into full Demon Form just to survive more than a day (let alone the hostile Idigam spirits). The God Machine would sense the demon before long, and send someone to pick him up. <br /> <br /> Still, lets say that former-angels-turned-flesh can produce essence somehow, and that the Idigam can feed on it. Suddenly, it has a shape... but we're still talking about it falling into Slumber. The demon just won't be around long enough. Can the Idigam new forms survive that long of a drought? Ciould they survive the journey back to Earth? <br /> <br /> Even if the Idigam could do all that, and somehow a demon could be imprsioned, I'm not sure what the difference that consolidating around a demon would be compared to doing the same when the Apolo first landed, and taking the human+machine essence as its guide. You'd have a bio-mechanical themed Idigam. I can't think of any major differences. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T10:28:22-07:00","id":649100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/631355-idigam-and-moon-invading-techno-demons?p=649096#post649096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, here's the thing about dropping a demon on the moon. It would die very quickly. Lets pretend that we have a Demonic Form part that lets it survive in Space (the Environmental Resistance should work). That still doesn't let the demon's human Cover survive for long - it still needs food and water. So, the Demon is forced to shift into full Demon Form just to survive more than a day (let alone the hostile Idigam spirits). The God Machine would sense the demon before long, and send someone to pick him up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could use an ephemeral cover.<br /> <br /> But look Piff wasn't asking, 'I have this idea for a background, please tell me how wrong you think it is.'<br /> <br /> The question was pretty clear, what would an idigam who placed its focus on a Demon be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:25:23-07:00","id":649172,"title":"","content":"Something to consider for this question: a demon not in Cover is a spiritual-esque entity that exists inherently in the flesh/mineral.<br /> <br /> Kind of like a Pangaean, from what we've read in the blogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-02-2015, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T08:56:50-07:00","id":650173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/631355-idigam-and-moon-invading-techno-demons?p=649172#post649172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to consider for this question: a demon not in Cover is a spiritual-esque entity that exists inherently in the flesh/mineral.<br /> <br /> Kind of like a Pangaean, from what we've read in the blogs.</div> </div> </div> </div> How do you figure that? Curious minds inquiring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:01:23-07:00","id":650267,"title":"","content":"Easy. We've been told a Pangaean is like a spiritual entity, but flesh.<br /> <br /> We've been told that the Unchained don't exactly have a soul you can fuck around with, because their physical bodies post-fall pretty much <i>are</i> their souls. So they are spiritual entity, but flesh(ish).*<br /> <br /> *And now I need go dig up the references that support this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T12:31:18-07:00","id":650448,"title":"","content":"A scenario which would underscore how estranged Demons are from the rest of reality could involve the following: No matter how it tries, the Idigam fails to &quot;read&quot; the Demon. To its senses, this entity is as spiritually sterile as the rest of the moon, offering nothing to coalesce around. This defies reason, since the Demon behaves in a consistent, complex manner and should reflect all kinds of concepts. After years of fruitless stalking, interrogation attempts and picking apart all traces of the guests activity, the Idigam coalesces around its own fascination, persistence and sense of failure, forever trying to solve this riddle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}